<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Assuwa</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 BCE – 1400 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Assuwa, a short-lived league of western Anatolian lands that rose against the Hittites c. 1430 BCE and may have given Asia its name.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Assuwa was a coalition of 22 lands in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilusa">Wilusiya</a> and Taruisa, often linked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>. It formed in the 15th century BCE in resistance to Hittite expansion westward.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known almost only from the annals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudhaliya-i">Tudhaliya I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>, the league was led by Piyama-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurunta">Kurunta</a> and his son Kukkuli. A bronze sword of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> type, inscribed with Tudhaliya's dedication after the victory over Assuwa, was found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> in 1991.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudhaliya-i">Tudhaliya I</a> defeated the coalition and deported thousands of soldiers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a>. Kukkuli rebelled again and was killed. The name may survive in the Greek and Roman name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1450 BCE – 1400 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:30.85%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 BCE – 1400 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century-bce">15th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Piyama-Kurunta, Kukkuli</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luwian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Assuwa League, Assuwan Confederacy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1425&amp;focus=assuwa" aria-label="Assuwa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5539 775 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Assuwa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5852 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5859 1031h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5859 1031h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Turkey. <a href="/atlas?year=-1425&amp;focus=assuwa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

